WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.940
World Masterpiece Theater

00:07.800 --> 00:14.400
Homeless Child Remy

00:07.800 --> 00:14.400
"About Love"

00:15.260 --> 00:23.200
I continue wishing to see you

00:23.690 --> 00:28.360
Today we'll go on a journey

00:28.450 --> 00:32.310
That's as endless as the blue sky

00:32.820 --> 00:40.990
With joy, sorrow and hope come setbacks

00:41.360 --> 00:46.040
They repeat, they repeat

00:46.280 --> 00:50.870
What should I believe?

00:51.510 --> 00:59.880
You know nothing about love, however

01:00.320 --> 01:08.900
Someday you will feel warmth inside

01:09.730 --> 01:19.860
I dream of the day when you'll speak of love

01:20.860 --> 01:28.660
Tomorrow, our journey will begin

01:29.510 --> 01:34.000
Presented by:
Takara Fansubs

01:35.030 --> 01:39.990
Episode 8:
Goodbye to Our Home

01:42.950 --> 01:44.410
Fire!

01:44.940 --> 01:46.480
Fire!

01:47.470 --> 01:49.170
This is the fifth fire!

01:49.520 --> 01:51.370
What are the police doing?

01:51.440 --> 01:53.160
They should arrest the culprits quickly!

01:53.200 --> 01:56.490
That's right, we can't sleep peacefully with this!

02:10.420 --> 02:12.360
Come everyone, the wait is over.

02:12.600 --> 02:17.690
The Italian trained Vitalis Troupe will now start performing their act.

02:39.470 --> 02:42.740
Amazing! Just amazing!
- So awesome!

02:42.770 --> 02:44.690
Wow, they're great.

02:53.420 --> 02:54.190
Step aside!

02:54.830 --> 02:55.530
Step aside!

02:55.890 --> 02:56.730
Step aside everyone.

02:58.750 --> 02:59.990
Stop the show.

03:00.210 --> 03:00.980
Everyone leave.

03:02.370 --> 03:06.580
Why? It's very strange to suddenly stop the show.

03:08.030 --> 03:09.310
What's that you...?

03:11.140 --> 03:12.000
That's enough, Remy.

03:12.130 --> 03:13.150
But...

03:13.940 --> 03:16.230
I'm the leader, Vitalis. What's the problem?

03:16.830 --> 03:19.910
There have been recent cases of arson.

03:20.110 --> 03:21.570
We are on alert.

03:22.230 --> 03:24.740
When did you arrive in Toulouse?

03:25.930 --> 03:27.450
A week ago.

03:27.740 --> 03:31.570
Oh? That was when the arson started.

03:33.230 --> 03:35.940
We're just doing our performances.

03:36.550 --> 03:42.370
I don't believe there is a law in Toulouse prohibiting street performers, is there?

03:44.380 --> 03:46.030
It's not like that!

03:46.300 --> 03:47.530
Leave, police!

03:48.480 --> 03:49.930
We want to see the show.

03:50.090 --> 03:52.690
Yeah! You must have spare time!

03:52.760 --> 03:54.650
Go catch the arsonists!

03:54.870 --> 03:58.110
Shut up! Everyone go home!

03:58.900 --> 04:01.150
It's illegal to have the carriage parked on the pavement.

04:02.030 --> 04:04.770
You'll have to go to the police station.

04:06.110 --> 04:08.490
Come, we'll go together.

04:08.870 --> 04:10.450
Wait, Mr. Policeman!

04:12.310 --> 04:15.000
They can park the carriage at my house.

04:17.420 --> 04:21.250
It doesn't matter if they dance and act there.

04:22.360 --> 04:24.430
Yeah! Mimi's right!

04:25.330 --> 04:28.040
The police have no power to ban a show.

04:28.350 --> 04:29.320
Yeah!

04:33.070 --> 04:35.010
Listen, I'm warning you!

04:35.320 --> 04:38.540
One wrong move and you'll be arrested immediately!

04:39.810 --> 04:41.840
An old man like me won't run or hide.

04:42.260 --> 04:43.780
He'll only perform.

04:47.700 --> 04:49.690
Hmmf... Hate that guy.

04:58.840 --> 05:00.400
Thanks so much.

05:00.560 --> 05:02.730
My name's Remy. What's yours?

05:02.890 --> 05:03.860
I'm Mimi.

05:04.150 --> 05:07.040
I'm really glad you came to my house.

05:07.120 --> 05:08.510
We're really no bother?

05:08.780 --> 05:12.350
It's fine. At the back of our shop is a big yard.

05:12.740 --> 05:14.750
My father will be happy to welcome you.

05:15.210 --> 05:17.750
Ah, I see, I see.

05:18.230 --> 05:19.950
I guess it can't be helped.

05:20.260 --> 05:22.970
You can put the carriage in the backyard.

05:23.150 --> 05:24.780
Thank you, sir.

05:25.400 --> 05:27.750
Just don't get into trouble.

05:28.240 --> 05:30.510
We understand. We'll be careful.

06:18.120 --> 06:18.650
Remy!

06:20.740 --> 06:22.000
What happened, Remy?

06:22.240 --> 06:24.950
Mr. Vitalis, a man suddenly ran out of nowhere.

06:26.230 --> 06:27.730
Fire!

06:33.310 --> 06:35.360
That person must have just been there.

06:36.190 --> 06:37.780
Remy, go back.

06:38.440 --> 06:40.100
Wait, I'm coming too.

06:47.020 --> 06:48.340
Hurry!

07:01.980 --> 07:03.460
The fire's been put out.

07:04.910 --> 07:06.020
Mr. Vitalis!

07:06.990 --> 07:08.990
Thank you very much.

07:10.250 --> 07:12.470
It's good there wasn't much damage.

07:12.630 --> 07:13.690
Move aside! Move aside!

07:16.240 --> 07:17.100
Huh?

07:17.680 --> 07:19.240
Of course it's you!

07:19.550 --> 07:21.110
You're the one responsible!

07:21.180 --> 07:24.490
What are you talking about?
He helped us put out the fire.

07:24.950 --> 07:28.960
Mr. Policeman! There was a man running away with jewelry.

07:29.290 --> 07:30.200
What?

07:30.460 --> 07:31.690
I saw him!

07:31.940 --> 07:33.900
That's it! He must be the culprit!

07:33.940 --> 07:37.160
Why aren't you going after him!?
- Hurry and catch him!

07:39.230 --> 07:40.200
All right.

07:40.930 --> 07:44.390
But, Mr. Vitalis, you have to be investigated.

07:44.830 --> 07:48.380
Listen, you can't leave town until you've been cleared.

07:48.730 --> 07:50.390
And you're still not allowed to perform.

07:50.960 --> 07:51.710
Understand!?

08:01.080 --> 08:03.920
The police seem to suspect you, Mr. Vitalis.

08:04.380 --> 08:05.950
I've done nothing.

08:06.340 --> 08:07.910
Don't worry.

08:08.480 --> 08:11.660
If we just ignore the police...

08:12.470 --> 08:16.660
Traveling performers will always be suspected.

08:18.780 --> 08:19.610
Really?

08:20.250 --> 08:23.760
Many people often judge by appearance or occupation.

08:25.610 --> 08:28.360
But the people here are really friendly.

08:28.650 --> 08:31.360
They helped us get rid of the police.

08:31.650 --> 08:33.190
And Mimi's father too.

08:34.560 --> 08:39.120
The truth will be revealed and the culprit will be caught.

08:39.720 --> 08:45.930
No matter what people say, the most important thing is to keep a clear conscience.

08:46.610 --> 08:50.030
Keep a clear conscience.

08:51.860 --> 08:53.200
Now, let's go to sleep.

08:53.710 --> 08:57.860
Since we can't perform, we'll take the chance to practice tomorrow.

09:11.700 --> 09:17.230
Though Mr. Vitalis doesn't seem to care, I want to catch the culprit.

09:17.430 --> 09:22.740
Me too. My father said the culprit is stealing things during the fire.

09:22.870 --> 09:24.390
He's a clever one.

09:25.030 --> 09:27.830
Uh, make the eyes smaller.

09:29.730 --> 09:30.650
Like that?

09:30.810 --> 09:34.250
Yeah, yeah. Just like that. Looks just like him.

09:34.310 --> 09:35.110
Really?

09:35.830 --> 09:38.100
Huh? This guy...

09:38.170 --> 09:39.140
You know him?

09:40.770 --> 09:42.230
Maybe I'm wrong.

09:49.610 --> 09:50.890
Don't know him.

10:02.550 --> 10:04.580
I'm tired.

10:05.390 --> 10:08.120
Say, we'll never find the culprit.

10:08.850 --> 10:13.190
He must be in town, I'm not giving up.

10:15.710 --> 10:17.400
Bye, thanks for your business.

10:17.510 --> 10:21.150
Next time, could you help me get some fashionable Paris lacework?

10:21.220 --> 10:24.990
I'll go order it.
- Great!

10:25.120 --> 10:27.370
Make sure to get them to me right away.

10:28.180 --> 10:29.440
Thank you.

10:30.120 --> 10:32.480
Take care, Mr. Naval.

10:32.590 --> 10:33.760
See you soon.

10:59.990 --> 11:01.640
Hi, Mr. Naval!

11:02.630 --> 11:04.990
Ah, Mimi. How are you?

11:05.120 --> 11:05.630
Good.

11:06.420 --> 11:07.020
Bye!

11:11.490 --> 11:12.350
It's him.

11:15.900 --> 11:18.060
That man's the culprit.

11:22.160 --> 11:26.330
But, my father knows him well.

11:26.700 --> 11:28.820
He said he's a real honest person.

11:30.010 --> 11:33.840
But there's no mistake, that man's the culprit.

11:41.850 --> 11:44.730
Hello, Mr. Vigor.
- Hello, Mr. Naval.

11:44.820 --> 11:48.170
I'd like to buy some ribbons today.
- Thank you for your business.

11:49.410 --> 11:52.380
Say, I just saw your daughter.

11:52.690 --> 11:55.340
She was with a girl I've never seen before.

11:56.750 --> 11:59.610
She's a traveling entertainer named Remy.

11:59.640 --> 12:01.990
They have their carriage parked behind the house.

12:03.620 --> 12:04.990
Behind the house?

12:09.620 --> 12:10.610
What should I do?

12:11.400 --> 12:14.690
It would be best to go to the police tomorrow.

12:15.190 --> 12:17.380
But will they believe me?

12:22.290 --> 12:23.020
What's wrong?

12:33.450 --> 12:34.860
Oh, no! Fire!

12:35.760 --> 12:38.140
Mimi, there's a fire! Wake up!

12:46.210 --> 12:48.900
It's terrible! The bakery is on fire!

13:00.360 --> 13:01.950
Mind your own business.

13:40.650 --> 13:43.380
Geez, finally the fire's out.

13:44.680 --> 13:45.430
Sandra!

14:00.020 --> 14:01.040
Sandra!

14:01.900 --> 14:04.540
It'll be okay! Good girl!

14:06.090 --> 14:06.810
There!

14:13.560 --> 14:16.950
Home! Our home!

14:28.060 --> 14:30.290
Ah! The shed!

14:34.630 --> 14:37.560
Quick! Put out the fire! Quick!

14:40.100 --> 14:42.610
Damn it! Damn it!

14:51.800 --> 14:55.390
Geez, they went too far this time.

14:56.940 --> 14:57.440
Hm?

15:00.750 --> 15:01.590
This is...

15:02.560 --> 15:04.080
My lamp...

15:04.920 --> 15:05.470
How did...

15:06.460 --> 15:07.740
Yours?

15:24.290 --> 15:25.720
I'll give you this.

15:26.910 --> 15:28.370
Thank you.

15:44.590 --> 15:45.160
Remy...

15:47.720 --> 15:48.840
Where's Sandra?

15:50.320 --> 15:52.970
The troupe needs money.

15:56.580 --> 15:58.390
Poor Sandra.

15:58.450 --> 16:04.210
Remy, no matter how painful, we must keep moving forward.

16:05.220 --> 16:07.230
Keep moving forward, Remy.

16:23.780 --> 16:24.730
You, Vitalis.

16:26.010 --> 16:29.840
You're under arrest on charges of arson on the bakery.

16:31.720 --> 16:34.070
You suspected me from the start.

16:34.650 --> 16:37.670
Regardless whether I'm guilty or not, you'll frame me as a criminal.

16:38.110 --> 16:41.720
Frame you? I'm not framing you.

16:41.850 --> 16:46.000
Your lamp was found in the burned warehouse. It's solid evidence.

16:46.150 --> 16:47.720
That money...

16:48.180 --> 16:49.770
Can also serve as evidence.

16:51.420 --> 16:53.740
I had to sell the donkey for money.

16:53.980 --> 16:55.120
Just go and ask.

16:55.720 --> 16:57.170
You'll be taken in for questioning.

16:57.350 --> 16:58.390
Now, seize him.

16:58.960 --> 17:00.720
Mr. Policeman, wait!

17:00.900 --> 17:03.540
I left the lamp in the yard.

17:03.720 --> 17:04.400
What?

17:04.730 --> 17:08.700
When the store was on fire, there must have been someone else who ran into the shed.

17:08.900 --> 17:10.920
It wasn't Mr. Vitalis.

17:11.300 --> 17:14.600
I know the name of the culprit.
You should arrest him

17:14.650 --> 17:16.510
His name's Naval.
- Watch what you say!

17:16.770 --> 17:18.270
Don't make false accusations!

17:20.050 --> 17:24.240
If someone's falsely accused you can be prosecuted!

17:24.680 --> 17:25.810
Go on.
- Yes, sir!

17:26.140 --> 17:27.920
No! No!

17:28.050 --> 17:30.170
Mr. Vitalis is innocent!
You can't take him away!

17:30.190 --> 17:32.150
You're a really loud little girl.

17:36.390 --> 17:39.430
These things...
- Stop it, step down.

17:42.980 --> 17:45.780
Please, don't hurt the little girl.

17:46.530 --> 17:49.520
Well, then be nice and come with us.

17:50.120 --> 17:53.950
No! Don't take Mr. Vitalis away!
- Remy...

17:54.370 --> 17:57.700
It's all right. The truth will eventually be revealed.

17:58.190 --> 17:59.290
Mr. Vitalis!
- Come on!

17:59.900 --> 18:01.010
Mr. Vitalis!

18:01.200 --> 18:03.320
Take care of everyone while I'm gone!

18:03.450 --> 18:04.840
Mr. Vitalis!

18:08.130 --> 18:10.240
Mr. Vitalis!

18:10.330 --> 18:12.470
Remy, I'm entrusting the troupe to you!

18:12.980 --> 18:14.980
Mr. Vitalis!

18:15.550 --> 18:16.280
Remy!

18:19.120 --> 18:21.110
Mr. Vitalis!

18:25.010 --> 18:27.500
Mr. Vitalis! Mr. Vitalis!

18:27.610 --> 18:29.990
How many times do I have to tell you!?

18:30.060 --> 18:32.830
You can't see Vitalis during an interrogation!

18:32.970 --> 18:35.880
Please! I have to see him! I have to see Mr. Vitalis!

18:35.940 --> 18:39.010
You really don't listen.
You're still being troublesome.

18:39.090 --> 18:40.700
Seeing Vitalis won't change anything.

18:47.800 --> 18:49.100
Look, it's them.

18:49.740 --> 18:52.800
That troupe's leader is guilty of arson.

18:53.860 --> 18:57.570
Poor thing.
- Don't go close to that child.

18:59.660 --> 19:01.070
Umm, I...

19:07.240 --> 19:10.110
You're still here!? Hurry and get out!

19:11.250 --> 19:14.960
Please let me stay here. I have to wait until Mr. Vitalis comes back.

19:15.090 --> 19:18.440
No. I can't let someone guilty of arson stay here.

19:18.660 --> 19:22.850
You're wrong! We didn't do anything, please believe me!

19:22.960 --> 19:25.730
I don't need more trouble. Hurry and leave.

19:28.270 --> 19:29.200
Mimi!

19:33.140 --> 19:34.130
Mimi...

19:45.070 --> 19:46.560
Look, it's them.

19:47.230 --> 19:49.300
Don't go close to that child.

19:51.080 --> 19:54.320
Remy, the truth will eventually be revealed.

19:54.870 --> 19:59.000
The most important thing is to keep a clear conscience.

20:02.370 --> 20:04.900
Remy, I'm entrusting the troupe to you!

20:08.890 --> 20:11.290
That's right, there's only one truth.

20:11.850 --> 20:13.850
Mr. Vitalis will be back.

20:14.250 --> 20:17.470
If I'm not strong then I can't move forward.

20:18.220 --> 20:19.140
But...

20:19.780 --> 20:24.260
But why? Why does no one believe me?

20:29.830 --> 20:31.290
Remy!

20:32.810 --> 20:34.150
Remy!

20:34.990 --> 20:35.540
Mimi!

20:38.450 --> 20:39.380
I'm sorry.

20:39.600 --> 20:43.370
I wanted to talk to you but father wouldn't allow it.

20:43.480 --> 20:46.560
Then you believe me, Mimi?

20:46.610 --> 20:47.710
Of course.

20:47.970 --> 20:50.900
Mr. Vitalis wouldn't have any reason to do that.

20:51.210 --> 20:54.670
The culprit is Naval. I believe you, Remy.

20:55.440 --> 20:56.720
Thank you, Mimi.

20:57.780 --> 21:01.530
I thought no one would believe us.

21:02.630 --> 21:05.450
Thank you. Thank you so much, Mimi.

21:06.270 --> 21:08.510
But now what will you do?

21:09.200 --> 21:12.480
I'll have to wait until Mr. Vitalis is free from this town...

21:12.550 --> 21:15.700
But, I can't stay here.

21:16.190 --> 21:21.120
Mimi, I'm sure when Mr. Vitalis is free he'll come look for you.

21:21.630 --> 21:22.030
Uh-huh.

21:22.890 --> 21:26.190
Tell him that Remy is fine and will send word.

21:28.480 --> 21:30.980
And will... send word.

21:32.210 --> 21:32.980
Remy!

21:35.120 --> 21:39.040
I believe the truth will be revealed.

21:38.980 --> 21:47.530
Try to love yourself more

21:39.770 --> 21:41.090
So until that day...

21:41.420 --> 21:42.660
My family...

21:43.010 --> 21:45.680
I must protect Mr. Vitalis' dear troupe.

21:48.630 --> 21:57.490
Abandoned dreams can be seen again

21:58.200 --> 22:06.600
Surely, not everyone can be so strong

22:07.870 --> 22:18.500
The blue sky lifts all of the world's tears...

22:19.200 --> 22:28.880
Tomorrow's courage comes

22:29.100 --> 22:38.730
From the future that gives us our fate

22:38.970 --> 22:47.000
Try to seek for them more

22:48.610 --> 22:52.130
Give your heart to

22:52.490 --> 23:07.170
That person who is also seeking you

23:20.270 --> 23:22.780
This isn't money, Joli-Coeur.

23:22.800 --> 23:23.840
This is my good-luck charm.

23:24.270 --> 23:26.380
Let me see Mr. Vitalis!

23:30.560 --> 23:32.980
I saw the real criminal's face!

23:32.980 --> 23:36.980
<i>Fateful Encounter</i>

23:32.980 --> 23:36.980
Next time:
